{
  "dom_id": "step-q87769",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178864/assets/c13c5ac52b7bc508032d2d53b1169730641bafefcd8c0f5487d96699d6120946.png)\n\nConsider the triangles $P$ and $Q$ shown above. Given that $WXY≅FGH,$ what is the perimeter of $Q?$",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $WXY≅FGH$ means that $P$ and $Q$ are congruent. Moreover,\n\n- vertex $W$ corresponds to vertex $F,$\n\n- vertex $X$ corresponds to vertex $G,$\n\n- vertex $Y$ corresponds to vertex $H.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FG & =WX \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}HF & =YW \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe figure shows that $FG=GH.$ Therefore, the perimeter of $Q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{Q} & =FG+GH+HF \\\\  & =5+5+5\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =5(2+\\sqrt{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
